  "note": "Van Eyck built color in layers of oil. The green dress is [[verdigris]], a copper green: opaque layers first, then a glaze of verdigris in oil and pine resin for depth. The bed hangings are [[vermilion-pigment|vermilion]], red lake and red earth under red glazes. The man's tabard, now almost [[Black|black]], was once a dark crimson-purple. Two old varnish layers survive, and the lower one has yellowed."
