  "note": "[[kandinsky|Kandinsky]] made more than 30 studies, then painted the final canvas in four days, 25 to 28 November 1913, while Gabriele Münter photographed each stage. In [[spiritual-in-art|Concerning the Spiritual in Art]] he compared color to a keyboard and the soul to a piano. Up close it is a clash of pure reds, yellows and blues; the swatches here are muddier because its patches are so small and so mixed."
